cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Thermodynamics.jl in your research, please cite the paper describing the
  formulation it implements.
title: Thermodynamics.jl
abstract: >-
  A Julia package for atmospheric moist thermodynamics, implementing the thermodynamic
  formulation of the CliMA Earth System Model. It provides thermodynamic functions for moist
  air including all phases of water, based on the Rankine-Kirchhoff approximations.
type: software
authors:
  - name: The Climate Modeling Alliance
repository-code: https://github.com/CliMA/Thermodynamics.jl
url: https://clima.github.io/Thermodynamics.jl/dev/
license: Apache-2.0
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    The Climate Modeling Alliance Atmosphere Dynamical Core: Concepts, Numerics, and Scaling
  journal: Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems
  year: 2026
  doi: 10.1029/2025MS005014
